CAT = "rshairClient"; SEG = "CLI"
# RSOS tasks A-3 (prepares for client services) and A-4 (communication and mentoring).
Q = [
("Which federal law governs how a salon collects and stores client personal information?",
 "PIPEDA", ["WHMIS", "Canada Labour Code", "Food and Drugs Act"],
 "The Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act sets the rules for collecting, using and storing personal information in private businesses. WHMIS covers hazardous products."),
("Which client feature guides the choice of a warm or cool hair colour?",
 "Skin tone", ["Face shape", "Hair density", "Growth pattern"],
 "Skin tone decides whether warm or cool shades flatter the client. Face shape guides the cut, and density and growth pattern guide sectioning and placement."),
("A client frowns and goes quiet while describing her last haircut. What is the stylist picking up on?",
 "Non-verbal cues", ["Verbal cues", "Active listening", "Paraphrasing"],
 "Facial expression, posture and silence are non-verbal communication, which the standard asks stylists to read as well as words. Verbal cues are spoken words, while active listening and paraphrasing are what the stylist does, not what the client shows."),
("For a chemical service, what goes between the client's neck and the cape?",
 "A towel or neck strip", ["A line of protective cream", "A cotton coil only", "A second waterproof cape"],
 "A barrier of towel or neck strip protects the skin and keeps the cape off the neck. Protective cream and cotton guard the hairline from drips, and a second cape adds no barrier against the skin."),
("Which cape suits a colour application best?",
 "Waterproof cape", ["Nylon cape", "Mesh cape", "Cotton cape"],
 "Waterproof capes keep liquid chemicals off clothing and skin. Nylon capes shed cut hair well but let liquids soak through."),
("Which salon document gives a colour's mixing ratio and processing time?",
 "Product instructions", ["Safety data sheet", "Colour chart", "Supplier label"],
 "Manufacturers' specifications and directions give mixing ratios and timing for each product. The safety data sheet covers hazards and first aid, the colour chart shows shades and the supplier label carries hazard warnings, not mixing ratios."),
("Which client feature mainly guides where length and volume go in a cut?",
 "Face shape", ["Eye colour", "Skin undertone", "Natural level"],
 "Face shape and profile guide where length and volume go in a cut. Eye colour, skin undertone and natural level guide colour choices instead."),
("After demonstrating a skill, what does a mentor provide next?",
 "Practice for the apprentice", ["A test for the apprentice", "Feedback for the apprentice", "A new lesson for the apprentice"],
 "The RSOS order is: state the point of the lesson, link it, demonstrate, set up practice conditions, then assess and give feedback. Assessment and feedback follow the practice."),
("An apprentice practises blow-drying with the mentor beside them giving tips. This is:",
 "Guided practice", ["Full independence", "Limited independence", "A probation review"],
 "Practice conditions run from guided, to limited independence, to full independence. A mentor at the chair coaching each step is guided practice."),
("An apprentice learns best by watching a colour mix first. Which learning style is this?",
 "Seeing it", ["Hearing it", "Trying it", "Writing it"],
 "The standard names three learning styles: seeing it, hearing it and trying it. Watching a demonstration is learning by seeing."),
("A coworker makes one demeaning remark about an apprentice's accent. How often must such remarks happen to count as harassment?",
 "Once is enough", ["Twice in a month", "Three or more times", "Only once reported"],
 "The RSOS defines harassment as objectionable conduct, comment or display, made once or repeatedly, that demeans or humiliates. It need not be repeated or in writing."),
("What does a stylist show a client to pick out a shade together?",
 "Swatch book", ["Safety data sheet", "Client waiver", "Price list"],
 "Swatch books and colour charts are used to select the colour the client wants. A waiver and price list are other salon documents."),
]
